{"task_id": "HumanEval/44", "solution": "def change_base(x: int, base: int):\n    \"\"\"Change numerical base of input number x to base.\n    return string representation after the conversion.\n    base numbers are less than 10.\n    >>> change_base(8, 3)\n    '22'\n    >>> change_base(8, 2)\n    '1000'\n    >>> change_base(7, 2)\n    '111'\n    \"\"\"\n    if x == 0:\n        return \"0\"\n\n    result = []\n    current_x = x\n    while current_x > 0:\n        remainder = current_x % base\n        result.append(str(remainder))\n        current_x //= base\n    \n    return \"\".join(result[::-1])"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "def fib4(n: int):\n    \"\"\"The Fib4 number sequence is a sequence similar to the Fibbonacci sequnece that's defined as follows:\n    fib4(0) -> 0\n    fib4(1) -> 0\n    fib4(2) -> 2\n    fib4(3) -> 0\n    fib4(n) -> fib4(n-1) + fib4(n-2) + fib4(n-3) + fib4(n-4).\n    Please write a function to efficiently compute the n-th element of the fib4 number sequence.  Do not use recursion.\n    >>> fib4(5)\n    4\n    >>> fib4(6)\n    8\n    >>> fib4(7)\n    14\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 2:\n        return 2\n    elif n == 3:\n        return 0\n    else:\n        # Store the last four Fib4 numbers [fib4(i-4), fib4(i-3), fib4(i-2), fib4(i-1)] for efficient computation.\n        fib4_values = [0, 0, 2, 0]  # Initial values for fib4(0), fib4(1), fib4(2), fib4(3).\n\n        for i in range(4, n + 1):\n            next_fib4 = fib4_values[3] + fib4_values[2] + fib4_values[1] + fib4_values[0]\n            # Update the sliding window: shift old values and add the new one.\n            fib4_values[0] = fib4_values[1]\n            fib4_values[1] = fib4_values[2]\n            fib4_values[2] = fib4_values[3]\n            fib4_values[3] = next_fib4\n        return fib4_values[3]"}
