{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "def median(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return median of elements in the list l.\n    >>> median([3, 1, 2, 4, 5])\n    3\n    >>> median([-10, 4, 6, 1000, 10, 20])\n    8.0\n    \"\"\"\n    sorted_l = sorted(l)\n    n = len(sorted_l)\n\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        # Odd number of elements: median is the middle element.\n        median_val = sorted_l[n // 2]\n    else:\n        # Even number of elements: median is the average of the two middle elements.\n        mid1 = sorted_l[n // 2 - 1]\n        mid2 = sorted_l[n // 2]\n        median_val = (mid1 + mid2) / 2.0\n    \n    # Return as int if it's a whole number, otherwise float.\n    return int(median_val) if median_val == int(median_val) else float(median_val)"}
